From f6eead1d15a9164f9159225208aef58bf26237d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:10:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] Parser: "the number of times it's been cast from the
 command zone this game"

Study Hall: "{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color. When you spend this
mana to cast your commander, scry X, where X is the number of times it's
been cast from the command zone this game."

CR 106.6 + CR 603.3: the spend trigger already parses for "your
commander"; only its X was missing, so the whole rider stayed an
unimplemented gap and casting the commander with Study Hall's mana never
scried. CR 903.8: the quantity is the command-zone cast count the
commander tax uses (QuantityRef::CommanderCastFromCommandZoneCount, as
for Opal Palace's "it enters with ... equal to the number of times it's
been cast from the command zone this game"). Like that form, it counts
the controller's command-zone casts, so with two commanders it counts
both.

Card data: the parse change reaches games only with card data generated
by this parser.

Tests: parser/oracle_nom/quantity.rs
test_parse_number_of_times_it_was_cast_from_the_command_zone and
parser/oracle_effect/mana.rs parses_study_hall_commander_scry_spend_trigger.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
